TestTypes: SDD

Purpose:
  Define the test types available in the system. Each test type has a
  specific purpose, scope, and ownership. AI selects applicable test
  types based on task impact, risk, and stack.

Owns: ./

Types:

  BDD:
    name: Behavior-Driven Development
    purpose: Define business behavior before implementation
    scope: business rules, user flows, acceptance criteria
    owner: Business/QA/Product
    format: Given/When/Then
    when: before implementation starts
    stack_agnostic: true
    first_class: true

  Unit:
    name: Unit Test
    purpose: Verify individual components in isolation
    scope: single function, method, class, component
    owner: Implementer
    frameworks:
      Go: testing, testify
      Laravel: PHPUnit
      Node: Jest, Vitest
      React: Jest, Vitest
      Vue: Vitest, Jest
    when: during implementation
    speed: fast

  Integration:
    name: Integration Test
    purpose: Verify components work together
    scope: API endpoints, database interactions, service calls
    owner: Implementer/QA
    frameworks:
      Go: testcontainers
      Laravel: PHPUnit + HTTP tests
      Node: Jest + supertest
    when: after unit tests pass
    speed: medium

  API:
    name: API Test
    purpose: Verify API contracts and behavior
    scope: REST/GraphQL/gRPC endpoints
    owner: QA/BE
    frameworks:
      Postman/Newman
      REST Assured
      Pact (contract testing)
    when: after BE stage
    speed: medium

  Contract:
    name: Contract Test
    purpose: Verify service-to-service contracts
    scope: API contracts, message schemas, event schemas
    owner: QA/BE
    frameworks:
      Pact
      Spring Cloud Contract
      Schemathesis
    when: after integration tests
    speed: medium

  E2E:
    name: End-to-End Test
    purpose: Verify complete user/business flows
    scope: full system, real dependencies
    owner: QA
    frameworks:
      Playwright
      Cypress
      Selenium
      Detox (mobile)
    when: before release
    speed: slow

  UI:
    name: UI Test
    purpose: Verify interface behavior
    scope: components, pages, user interactions
    owner: FE/QA
    frameworks:
      React: Testing Library, Cypress
      Vue: Vue Test Utils, Cypress
      Angular: Jasmine, Cypress
    when: during FE implementation
    speed: medium

  Mobile:
    name: Mobile Test
    purpose: Verify mobile app behavior
    scope: native features, gestures, offline behavior
    owner: MD/QA
    frameworks:
      React Native: Jest, Detox
      Flutter: flutter_test, integration_test
      iOS: XCTest
      Android: Espresso
    when: during MD implementation
    speed: slow

  Performance:
    name: Performance Test
    purpose: Verify system performance meets NFRs
    scope: response time, throughput, resource usage
    owner: QA/DO
    frameworks:
      k6
      Gatling
      JMeter
      Lighthouse
    when: before production
    speed: varies

  Load:
    name: Load Test
    purpose: Verify system behavior under expected load
    scope: concurrent users, request rates, sustained load
    owner: QA/DO
    frameworks:
      k6
      Gatling
      JMeter
      Locust
    when: before production
    speed: slow

Selection:
  AI MUST select test types based on:
    Task impact (from task ImpactMatrix)
    Task risk (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL)
    Stack (BE/FE/MD/DB/INFRA)
    Security level (L0-L5)
    Project scale

  Not all test types apply to every task:
    DB-only task: Unit, Integration
    FE task: Unit, UI, E2E
    MD task: Unit, Mobile, E2E
    BE task: Unit, Integration, API
    Infrastructure: Load, Performance

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Workflow: @t-levels.sdd
  TestLevels: @levels.sdd
  TestGates: @gates.sdd
  BDD: @bdd.sdd
  Unit: @unit.sdd
  Integration: @integration.sdd
  API: @api.sdd
  Contract: @contract.sdd
  E2E: @e2e.sdd
  UI: @ui.sdd
  Mobile: @mobile.sdd
  Performance: @performance.sdd
  Load: @load.sdd
  ProjectTesting: @projects/{project_name}/testing/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  Note:
  Test types are stack-agnostic principles. Adapters for specific
  languages/frameworks are selected at execution time based on
  PROJECT.sdd -> Stack. This keeps testing knowledge reusable
  across projects.
